            <ArticleTitle>Review article: management of acute severe and near-fatal asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-68</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1742-6723.2009.01195.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite a decline in the Australian overall asthma mortality, near-fatal/critical asthma continues to be a significant management issue for emergency physicians and intensivists. Near-fatal asthma is a unique subtype of asthma, with a variety of clinical presentations, requiring rapid and aggressive intervention. The pharmacological and non-pharmacological management of near-fatal asthma remains very complex. The present review discusses recent advances and evidence for current available strategies targeting this time critical emergency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
